Z||000003||theogre||10-21-2000||06:21 PM||||I think T5 was used by GM on the back end of V6's in Old's HO version of the Monza in the late 70's early 80's. It was a Borg Warner 5 speed at any rate. I'm not sure if it was T5 or another one. Haven't seen one in years.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||10-21-2000||09:28 PM||||The late 70's - early 80's GM 5 speed was a T-50. Had one in a 77 Starfire. Hated it. It was set up like a 3-speed, with reverse right above 1st, 2 and 3 in the middle, 4 and 5 on the right. Big pain in the ass to drive, especially with the mushy motormounts that GM used on the 3.8 (<I>not</I> 3800) to try to dampen the vibration. <BR>There was a T-5 in a Nissan?!? Which one?<BR>If so, my gut feeling says they won't bolt up to a GM or Ford, at all. Having said that, I'm probably dead wrong.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
