Z||000014||Pontiaddict||10-23-2000||09:31 PM||||I'm guessing that due to the v8 swaps they do to Nissans, that some parts are interchangeable. I know that the bellhousings do not interchange between Chevy and Ford. <P>I'll say that it'll work with a Chevy. A 2.5/2.8 if anything.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Xtreme Fiero's||10-23-2000||11:29 PM||||First & formost MY NISSAN 300ZX powerd Hardbody Pickip is NOT A RICER!!!! It pisses mo off when stupid fools say Ricer or Rice Burner. You are a idiot if you realy think ALL imports suck. You don't even now what Ricer means. It is raceist and rude. You here Nissan and assume it is covered with stickers, Does your Ferrari body kist make your Fiero go Faster? NOPE! It even slows it down with drag & weight, You just thnk it looks good. Well I like The Touring car look, and you like the look of a wanabe.<P>FIEROCIOUS: My trans will fit I will need a new Bell houseing, Inputshaft & Tail<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000016||Wannabe||10-24-2000||08:10 AM||||I don't know if they all used the same input shaft dimensions or bell housing mounts, but the T5 tranny, made by Borg-Warner, was used in the the V8 Mustang, the V8 Camaros & Firebirds, and the 300ZX, starting with the 5.0 Mustang in '83, it's first use behind a v8. It evolved from the transmission used in the Monza/Sunbird in the early eighties. The cases may be slightly different between the various applications, but the internals, except for different gear ratios, are the same. What the toploader has to do with it I'm not sure. The toploader was Ford's 4 speed, going back at least as far as the first 289 Mustangs, and as far as I know, has nothing in common with the T5.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Greg Piet||10-24-2000||03:34 PM||||Please breathe in.<BR>I do not think anyone needs to get all ruffled up about someone calling a Japanese import "Rice".<P>I even call MY Japanese motorcycle a "Rice Bike"...  I jokingly say it is powered by Kikoman...<P>Everything will be cool baby...  chill man, chill.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000018||rockcrawl||10-24-2000||07:47 PM||||Xtreme Fiero's,<BR> Was that post directed toward me? Just in case it was, and it really sounds like it was, I must defend myself. The term "Rice-burner" was around long before the vynil stickers and huge wings were in effect. I call any vehicle from Japan a rice-burner, weather it's modified or bone stock. My '91 ZX6 Ninja is a rice-burner. I don't think all imports suck. I do prefer to drive american made cars. I wish I could afford Italian made cars. I am a mechanic for a Toyota dealer. My stand on racism has nothing to do with my opinion of your Nissan! I think it's cool that you have a Z engine in your truck, but it really doesn't interest me, <B>I'm not into rice</B><P> And about the kit body, well, here we go. I spent $12,000 to build a Countach replica with a 350 TPI engine. It weighed 2910 lbs with a full tank. Added drag and weight??? I think not. It was faster and lighter that a Fiero. I sold the car for $30,000 two days after I posted the ad. I could have sold it ten times over within the following two weeks. Obviously there are a lot of people who like the wanabe look as you call it. I have a hard time selling stock Fieros, not to mention trying to make any profit on them.<P>Like Greg said, chill man, chill, and to each his own!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
