Z||000020||Pontiaddict||10-25-2000||11:37 PM||||FIEROCIOUS, I missed your clues. It'd be the ford stuff that fits then. (If that's why you put top loader as a clue)<P><BR>I know that the bellhousing to trans bolt pattern is different between Chevy and Ford and that the respective bolt patterns are rotated in relation to a normal four speed. I guessed wrong the first time.<P><BR>PS: When I hear Nissan I think about their new truck with the 200hp supercharged V6 (as opposed to the 180hp non blown engine) along with all of the other crap in their commercials.<P><BR>Here's some more auto trivia.<P>Which car was faster (1/4 mile) from the factory*<BR>A '64 GTO or a '64 Catalina?<BR>*as tested by Motor Trend||||reg||1
Z||000021||FIEROCIOUS||10-27-2000||01:30 AM||||OK rockcrawl, He He He you "thought" you got me huh? well it does say (water) thermostat the picture you posted in no way controls water temperature!<P>The T-5 for a Camaro is off-set relative to center as opposed to the ford T-5 strait up position. A T-5 is a toploader transmission as are all tranies with the linkage mounted inside on top. I don't know if the nissan T-5 is compatable with chevy but I'd sure like to know!<P>Let me guess? the Catalina was faster by just a bit?<BR>  ||||reg||1
